<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hacı I Giray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Haji I Giray, Haci I Giray, Hadji Giray</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hacı I Giray was the founder of the Crimean Khanate and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giray-dynasty">Giray dynasty</a>, which ruled it until 1783. A descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> through Jochi, he established an independent khanate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> around 1441 with Lithuanian support, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> broke apart. He allied with Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> against the Great Horde and died in 1466.</p></div>
